---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Source">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Open implementation</span>
    <h1>Inspect the benchmark, not just the chart.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Tasks, test cases, schemas, scoring code, release locks, and published
      result manifests are available in the public repository.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button" href="https://github.com/Carrick-K7/carrick-ai-gamebench">Open GitHub</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/methodology">Read methodology</a>
    </div>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="grid cols-3">
        <article class="card">
          <span class="pill">Benchmark</span>
          <h3>Tasks and release locks</h3>
          <p>Prompts, references, state schemas, deterministic cases, point weights, and immutable catalog hashes.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="pill">Evaluator</span>
          <h3>Runner and browser tests</h3>
          <p>Shell-neutral Agent execution, controlled browser evaluation, evidence manifests, and score aggregation.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="pill">Results</span>
          <h3>Clean public artifacts</h3>
          <p>Published source excludes logs, trajectories, environment files, credentials, caches, and provider responses.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section prose">
      <h2>Licensing</h2>
      <p>
        GameBench code is Apache-2.0. Reproduce tasks retain their upstream
        license, exact commit, copyright notices, and distributed-material
        hashes. A public artifact never broadens the license of upstream work.
      </p>
      <h2>Security boundary</h2>
      <p>
        Agent-generated game JavaScript is not trusted application code. Public
        playables run on an isolated origin with a restrictive CSP and without
        access to the main site's storage or document.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
